    "notes": [
      "The POSIX-only module deliberately asserts the POSIX gate; select it only on Linux.",
      "Donor catalog and backup cases are adapted to the current API and actual fragment/native5 contracts. All donor scenario families remain; three actual cancellation/restart controls are added.",
      "The positive cancellation fixture alone inserts a scoped bootstrap hold after the real atomic readiness acknowledgment. The measured harness never inserts a delay.",
      "Existing 60-second slice, 120/180-second test calls and actual child ownership remain. All added cases retain the same existing stage/cancellation limits.",
      "One additional measured 65 MiB private runtime input checks the real conservative caller accounting against core _copy_allowance. It does not claim that this input was imported or archived.",
      "The selected-worker exit-7 negative proves that a failed/quarantined row cannot be relabeled as an unmeasured cancellation; no cancellation report is published."
    ]
  },
  "implementation": {
    "reuse": [
      "Unchanged bounded donor generator and its two guard suites.",
      "Current LibraryApp plan_import_page/continue_import_scan/run_import_batch/resume_import, saved TextProfile2 and v3 batch records.",
      "Current ResourceBroker and exact audio.process.run_process(owned_tree=True), with only per-worker metrics/readiness prefix before the same verified worker entry.",
      "Current search_page/federated pages and authoritative quote copy; no donor search/index implementation.",
      "Current native5 typed-sidecar backup with caller-selected BackupBudget, independent original/raw/full-table oracle and passive restore."
    ],
    "reconciliation": [
      "Real 65536-character fragments replace donor whole-field fragment assumptions.",
      "The current catalog.registration and storage.revisions modules provide publication identity; no nonexistent storage.publication module is imported.",
      "The large-field tests independently compute all actual fragments and prove exact final-field navigation past the first source window.",
      "BOM bytes count in the original allowance; decoded field bytes use the actual explicit segment guard.",
      "No nonexistent LibraryApp.close_search, donor max_items/slice_items, SearchResources or search.paging call remains.",
      "Current native5 is required using a genuine typed keybinding sidecar; supported flat4 is explicitly a separate existing compatibility gate.",
      "Cancellable retained-source resolution uses the same outer deadline.",
      "The complete declared archive-data bound is doubled, alongside two manifests and the existing 64 MiB margin, matching current core _copy_allowance and _staging_requirement before any archive exists.",
      "Failed, quarantined or excluded cancellation rows remain failures. A completed-before-cancellation reason requires a positive selected-worker completion record; otherwise the boundary is explicitly unproved."
    ],
    "measurement_limits": [
      "Synthetic 1000/10000/50000-book and large-original tiers are requested, never inferred from small tests.",
      "Current measured disk and available physical/cgroup memory can refuse a tier; generator returns NOT_RUN/code2 and catalog/backup return NOT_RUN/code3.",
      "Per-worker own-process exit peaks and coordinator peaks are separately labeled. Simultaneous family peak and OS memory enforcement are NOT_MEASURED.",
      "Killed-child peak is NOT_MEASURED; cancellation requires actual startup acknowledgment, actual native AudioCancelled, saved canceled row and unchanged IDs.",
      "Global ranking, semantic/private models, physical audio and human/NVDA quality are not qualified.",
      "Selected script/module hashes are emitted and compared. The existing receiving workflow must separately prove the full 398-module installed/source namespace; this harness does not claim that selected-module hashes prove it.",
      "Every import/catalog integrity pass remains real. A time-limited or incomplete tier is not capacity acceptance."
    ]
  },
